      "problem": "Find the missing values in the following truth table:",
      "worked_solution": "According to the definition of the biconditional, \n\n- $P⇔Q$ is true if $P⇒Q$ **and** $Q⇒P.$ Otherwise, it is false.\n\n- In other words, $P⇔Q$ is true if $P$ and $Q$ have the same truth values. Otherwise, it is false.\n\nFirst, we add a columns for $X∨Y$ and $¬(X∨Y):$\n\n| $\\,X\\,$ | $\\,Y\\,$ | $\\,X∨Y\\,$ | $\\,¬(X∨Y)\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n\nFinally, we add a column for $¬(X∨Y)⇔X.$ \n\n| $\\,X\\,$ | $\\,Y\\,$ | $\\,X∨Y\\,$ | $\\,¬(X∨Y)\\,$ | $\\,¬(X∨Y)⇔X\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ |",
